WEBVTT

00:00:01.650 --> 00:00:03.919
Do you know
about Season Fairies?

00:00:03.919 --> 00:00:06.455
They make the rain fall.
They make the wind blow.

00:00:06.455 --> 00:00:07.857
They make clouds.

00:00:07.857 --> 00:00:11.122
They're little fairies
who govern the seasons.

00:00:11.293 --> 00:00:13.028
But... can you believe it?

00:00:13.028 --> 00:00:16.759
It tumbled into my
room, of all places!

00:00:17.433 --> 00:00:18.801
Are you listening
to me, Sugar?

00:00:18.801 --> 00:00:21.303
Yeah, more importantly,
what about Mr. Bear?

00:00:21.303 --> 00:00:23.066
That's not more important!

00:00:24.006 --> 00:00:27.376
Sugar Baby Love

00:00:27.376 --> 00:00:30.513
Kuchibiru ni

00:00:30.513 --> 00:00:34.142
Namida no rouge

00:00:55.104 --> 00:00:58.641
Sugar Baby Love

00:00:58.641 --> 00:01:06.070
Ai nante, Shiritaku naiwa

00:01:09.652 --> 00:01:13.122
Sugar Baby Love

00:01:13.122 --> 00:01:16.158
Kuchibiru ni

00:01:16.158 --> 00:01:19.650
Namida no rouge

00:01:24.033 --> 00:01:27.703
Mokuyo ni

00:01:27.703 --> 00:01:30.706
Bara o kai

00:01:30.706 --> 00:01:34.142
Tegami o soete

00:01:38.447 --> 00:01:42.084
Sugar Baby Love

00:01:42.084 --> 00:01:45.087
Yume de au

00:01:45.087 --> 00:01:49.615
Anata wa yasashii

00:01:59.168 --> 00:02:02.771
Sniff. Sniff... Gulp...

00:02:02.771 --> 00:02:03.965
How is it?

00:02:04.139 --> 00:02:05.003
Good?

00:02:05.608 --> 00:02:08.042
It's somehow stiff-tasting.

00:02:09.545 --> 00:02:15.484
It's somehow stiff-tasting...

00:02:16.952 --> 00:02:22.117
It's somehow stiff-tasting...

00:02:22.591 --> 00:02:24.718
I... I can't breathe!

00:02:28.631 --> 00:02:30.792
A-a dream?

00:02:34.403 --> 00:02:35.927
Mr. Bear...

00:02:35.971 --> 00:02:36.903
Hey.

00:02:41.477 --> 00:02:46.073
"Stiff-tasting."
What does that mean?

00:02:47.483 --> 00:02:49.974
I just don't know...

00:02:55.925 --> 00:02:58.826
Oh, no!
I'll be late for Little Me!

00:02:59.128 --> 00:03:01.096
Wait, Saga!

00:03:01.096 --> 00:03:02.631
What was that yesterday?

00:03:02.631 --> 00:03:04.500
The dead bear
came back to life.

00:03:04.500 --> 00:03:07.102
The sun was shining,
and then it even snowed.

00:03:07.102 --> 00:03:08.971
Is it some type of magic?

00:03:08.971 --> 00:03:12.074
I told you!
That's what a play is.

00:03:12.074 --> 00:03:14.109
Now let go of me!

00:03:14.109 --> 00:03:16.712
But I don't understand
what a play is!

00:03:16.712 --> 00:03:18.475
Just explain it to us, please!

00:03:19.248 --> 00:03:21.250
Oh! A flying waffle!

00:03:21.250 --> 00:03:23.115
Huh? Where? Waffo?

00:03:23.619 --> 00:03:25.484
She's gone.

00:03:25.654 --> 00:03:28.122
Huh?
Ooh, Saga!

00:03:29.358 --> 00:03:31.827
Those kids sure are persistent.

00:03:31.827 --> 00:03:32.759
Saga?

00:03:34.797 --> 00:03:36.492
Anne! Norma!

00:03:37.766 --> 00:03:40.135
What? You're going to
see the play again?

00:03:40.135 --> 00:03:41.067
Yeah!

00:03:41.704 --> 00:03:43.399
That play sure is popular.

00:03:43.572 --> 00:03:44.368
Huh?

00:03:44.607 --> 00:03:45.574
Hmm?
Nothing.

00:03:45.574 --> 00:03:49.078
What do you like
about it so much?

00:03:49.078 --> 00:03:54.516
I've fallen in love with the
actor who the bear turns into!

00:04:00.089 --> 00:04:02.958
I have something to tell you.

00:04:02.958 --> 00:04:03.993
What is it?

00:04:03.993 --> 00:04:07.396
I can only stay in
human at night.

00:04:07.396 --> 00:04:11.100
No one can stop
these feelings.

00:04:11.100 --> 00:04:14.436
So I'm going to see it
as many times as I can!

00:04:14.436 --> 00:04:15.926
I... I see.

00:04:16.271 --> 00:04:18.641
I thought I'd like to
see it once more.

00:04:18.641 --> 00:04:22.008
That's why I'm going
today with Norma.

00:04:23.112 --> 00:04:25.444
Hey, Saga,
do you want to come?

00:04:25.781 --> 00:04:26.448
Huh?

00:04:26.448 --> 00:04:28.717
Well, it is a story
about a pianist!

00:04:28.717 --> 00:04:31.854
Your mother was a pianist,
wasn't she?

00:04:31.854 --> 00:04:34.516
But that's just a play.

00:04:35.057 --> 00:04:37.292
A real pianist is
totally different.

00:04:37.292 --> 00:04:39.192
I wonder if that's true.

00:04:39.395 --> 00:04:40.191
It is!

00:04:40.462 --> 00:04:43.056
A real pianist...

00:04:45.501 --> 00:04:52.873
enchants everyone with their
beautiful and gentle piano playing.

00:04:53.876 --> 00:04:57.346
Now that you mention it,
you play like that, too, Saga.

00:04:57.346 --> 00:04:59.682
Like when you
play at school.

00:04:59.682 --> 00:05:00.944
Really?

00:05:03.419 --> 00:05:05.614
Good grief,
this is sudden!

00:05:05.821 --> 00:05:07.083
What is it?

00:05:07.489 --> 00:05:08.820
I just had a phone call.

00:05:09.124 --> 00:05:10.893
Apparently they heard
of our reputation.

00:05:10.893 --> 00:05:13.726
They placed an rush order
for coffee for thirty people.

00:05:14.029 --> 00:05:15.462
From whom?

00:05:16.265 --> 00:05:17.433
The Hammond Theater Troupe!

00:05:17.433 --> 00:05:18.634
What?

00:05:18.634 --> 00:05:21.737
We were just
talking about them.

00:05:21.737 --> 00:05:22.738
Right, Norma?

00:05:22.738 --> 00:05:23.830
Yeah, yeah.

00:05:33.048 --> 00:05:34.950
Mr. Luchino, I'll go.

00:05:34.950 --> 00:05:37.052
Huh? Will you be
all right alone?

00:05:37.052 --> 00:05:38.041
Yes.

00:05:41.457 --> 00:05:44.126
Before the show you
can go backstage, right?

00:05:44.126 --> 00:05:45.127
Huh?

00:05:45.127 --> 00:05:47.118
Hey, Saga,
can I go with you?

00:05:47.362 --> 00:05:49.922
It's my chance to
get closer to him!

00:05:50.299 --> 00:05:51.630
Show some restraint, Norma.

00:05:51.900 --> 00:05:54.136
Saga's going for work.

00:05:54.136 --> 00:05:56.468
Yeah, I know.

00:05:56.672 --> 00:05:57.502
Sorry.

00:05:58.841 --> 00:05:59.500
What?

00:05:59.875 --> 00:06:02.139
You want to know
what a play is?

00:06:02.444 --> 00:06:03.342
Yes!

00:06:06.682 --> 00:06:08.684
The Elder's thinking.

00:06:08.684 --> 00:06:11.517
The Elder will know.
I'm sure of it.

00:06:14.857 --> 00:06:18.122
Oh, what a touching play.

00:06:18.293 --> 00:06:20.395
I'm so sad today.

00:06:20.395 --> 00:06:22.464
I can't stand to be alone!

00:06:22.464 --> 00:06:25.331
It's all right.
I'm here for you...

00:06:26.535 --> 00:06:27.536
All right!

00:06:27.536 --> 00:06:28.904
Elder!!

00:06:28.904 --> 00:06:29.962
Do you know?

00:06:31.507 --> 00:06:34.176
Ginger!

00:06:34.176 --> 00:06:38.010
I'm going to invite
you to the play.

00:06:39.314 --> 00:06:40.849
He's gone.

00:06:40.849 --> 00:06:43.443
The mystery gets
deeper and deeper.

00:06:44.086 --> 00:06:47.419
But to leave it
as a mystery?

00:06:48.223 --> 00:06:50.350
Then what should we do?

00:06:53.962 --> 00:06:54.963
Hey, Saga.

00:06:54.963 --> 00:06:56.658
I can't help!
See you later!

00:06:56.999 --> 00:06:59.763
Why's she in such a hurry?

00:07:00.536 --> 00:07:03.038
Sorry to keep you waiting.
I'm from Little Me!

00:07:03.038 --> 00:07:05.140
Oh, from the coffee shop.
Go around back.

00:07:05.140 --> 00:07:06.129
Ok.

00:07:09.311 --> 00:07:12.144
So, this is what it's
like before a play starts.

00:07:13.248 --> 00:07:15.284
Oh, are you from
the coffee shop?

00:07:15.284 --> 00:07:16.148
Oh, yes!

00:07:16.585 --> 00:07:17.886
Come here!

00:07:17.886 --> 00:07:22.324
Hey, everyone, coffee's here!
Let's have a drink.

00:07:22.324 --> 00:07:23.518
All right.

00:07:26.929 --> 00:07:28.163
Here you go.

00:07:28.163 --> 00:07:28.686
Thank you.

00:07:40.876 --> 00:07:42.036
Here you go.

00:07:43.745 --> 00:07:44.734
You are...

00:07:46.281 --> 00:07:48.306
Huh?
Stiff-tasting?

00:07:48.851 --> 00:07:52.878
Yes. I've been wondering
about what you said, and...

00:07:53.121 --> 00:07:54.952
Did I say that?

00:07:56.124 --> 00:07:59.582
Hey!
I'm serious!

00:08:05.100 --> 00:08:07.364
How does it taste?

00:08:08.136 --> 00:08:11.572
It's not bad, but...

00:08:11.907 --> 00:08:12.908
But?

00:08:12.908 --> 00:08:16.139
It's sort of
a little bit stiff-tasting.

00:08:16.545 --> 00:08:17.842
Sorry, sorry...

00:08:18.013 --> 00:08:20.345
I remember, but that was...

00:08:23.652 --> 00:08:26.314
I changed the blend
a little bit today.

00:08:26.455 --> 00:08:27.723
So how is it?

00:08:27.723 --> 00:08:30.157
Is it still, you know,
"stiff-tasting"?

00:08:34.196 --> 00:08:38.030
What I'm trying to say is that was
something off the top of my head.

00:08:38.233 --> 00:08:40.428
There wasn't any
deep meaning to it.

00:08:40.636 --> 00:08:42.104
Is that so?

00:08:42.104 --> 00:08:43.105
I mean,

00:08:43.105 --> 00:08:45.340
I don't know
how to say this,

00:08:45.340 --> 00:08:47.638
but I wasn't really thinking.

00:08:54.383 --> 00:08:57.113
Maybe it wasn't anything
to take seriously.

00:08:57.686 --> 00:09:01.486
I know. Since we're on break,
we should have some music.

00:09:02.524 --> 00:09:04.458
Vincent, play something.

00:09:04.826 --> 00:09:06.123
Any requests?

00:09:06.561 --> 00:09:07.585
I'll leave it to you.

00:09:09.131 --> 00:09:10.120
Well, then.

00:09:13.135 --> 00:09:18.573
In the style of Ingrid Bergman,
a musician raised in this town...

00:09:47.636 --> 00:09:49.103
His piano playing...

00:09:51.106 --> 00:09:52.835
His piano playing is

00:09:54.109 --> 00:09:56.270
just like my mom...

00:10:09.391 --> 00:10:12.724
We asked Saga and Elder,
and we still don't understand.

00:10:13.028 --> 00:10:14.296
That means!

00:10:14.296 --> 00:10:18.367
We'll just have to investigate
and solve the mystery ourselves.

00:10:18.367 --> 00:10:21.859
That's what we'll do, Salt and
Pepper! What a good idea!

00:10:22.137 --> 00:10:23.138
Salt, too.

00:10:23.138 --> 00:10:24.298
Q-Quit it.

00:10:25.140 --> 00:10:27.131
Oh. Wait, Salt!

00:11:07.149 --> 00:11:09.384
Oh, that was great.

00:11:09.384 --> 00:11:11.353
Ok, now let's get ready.

00:11:11.353 --> 00:11:12.411
Ok!

00:11:14.022 --> 00:11:15.457
That was surprising.

00:11:15.457 --> 00:11:16.048
Huh?

00:11:16.758 --> 00:11:19.522
I didn't know you
could play like that.

00:11:20.062 --> 00:11:23.632
I only knew how you
played as the bear.

00:11:23.632 --> 00:11:24.428
Yeah,

00:11:25.000 --> 00:11:26.797
Ingrid Bergman

00:11:27.469 --> 00:11:30.097
is one of my
favorite pianists.

00:11:30.372 --> 00:11:31.964
She's from this town.

00:11:32.074 --> 00:11:33.141
Do you know her?

00:11:33.141 --> 00:11:35.609
Huh?
Ah, yeah, well...

00:11:36.878 --> 00:11:40.075
She's my role model.

00:11:40.782 --> 00:11:41.771
Yeah.

00:11:44.086 --> 00:11:46.020
She's a wonderful person.

00:11:48.590 --> 00:11:51.626
Oh, Miss Saga!
What are you doing here?

00:11:51.626 --> 00:11:54.229
Greta?
Wh-What about you?

00:11:54.229 --> 00:11:59.098
Actually, when I talked about
this theater troupe to my father,

00:12:00.602 --> 00:12:02.695
somehow he made
me a member!

00:12:02.838 --> 00:12:05.102
I said it wasn't
necessary, but...

00:12:08.877 --> 00:12:13.515
Well, the time for me to bloom
as an actress has finally come.

00:12:13.515 --> 00:12:17.246
A new star will be
born here today!

00:12:18.086 --> 00:12:20.155
Yes, that's me.

00:12:20.155 --> 00:12:22.623
So, what role is it?

00:12:23.091 --> 00:12:24.888
The hunter's assistant.

00:12:28.130 --> 00:12:29.927
It... it might be a small role now,

00:12:30.098 --> 00:12:34.136
but once they see me,
they'll give me a better role!

00:12:34.136 --> 00:12:36.127
Well, just watch.

00:12:37.672 --> 00:12:39.341
I wonder if she'll be all right.

00:12:39.341 --> 00:12:41.172
Well, it'll work out somehow.

00:12:43.912 --> 00:12:45.747
Fifteen minutes
'til show time!

00:12:45.747 --> 00:12:46.543
Get ready.

00:12:47.082 --> 00:12:49.312
Oh, it's time already?

00:12:52.587 --> 00:12:53.747
Oh, um...

00:12:56.558 --> 00:12:58.753
Please do your
best in the play.

00:12:59.161 --> 00:13:00.150
Thanks.

00:13:06.434 --> 00:13:09.426
Ok, and this is everything.

00:13:13.041 --> 00:13:14.269
No way.

00:13:15.610 --> 00:13:17.100
Oh, no!
It's them.

00:13:18.847 --> 00:13:21.583
Somehow it seems different
from the last time we were here.

00:13:21.583 --> 00:13:24.108
It's supposed to be
the same place, though.

00:13:24.419 --> 00:13:27.756
At any rate,
let's investigate!

00:13:27.756 --> 00:13:28.882
Yeah!

00:13:34.296 --> 00:13:36.965
I've never seen
a play before!

00:13:36.965 --> 00:13:38.133
I can't wait.

00:13:38.133 --> 00:13:39.065
Hey, hey!

00:13:39.534 --> 00:13:42.332
Not so close!
Honestly!

00:13:43.071 --> 00:13:47.735
Ginger invited Turmeric, when it
was supposed to be just us.

00:13:53.181 --> 00:13:55.016
Oh! A window!

00:13:55.016 --> 00:13:56.005
Waffo!

00:13:57.085 --> 00:13:59.645
This isn't a real window.

00:13:59.788 --> 00:14:04.054
This chimney is fake, too.
It's just a picture.

00:14:04.359 --> 00:14:06.987
Does a play mean
you use paper?

00:14:09.431 --> 00:14:12.100
I still don't understand.

00:14:12.100 --> 00:14:15.092
Ok, more investigating!

00:14:17.105 --> 00:14:18.504
Oh, no!!

00:14:22.077 --> 00:14:24.613
Hey!
You guys!

00:14:24.613 --> 00:14:26.414
And now The Hammond
Theater Troupe

00:14:26.414 --> 00:14:29.117
will give a special performance
of "The Bear Pianist."

00:14:29.117 --> 00:14:31.686
Please take your seats.

00:14:31.686 --> 00:14:32.675
Huh, already?

00:14:42.397 --> 00:14:46.026
I have to catch Sugar and them
before they ruin the play!

00:14:52.874 --> 00:14:56.645
Grandma, what is
that piano sound?

00:14:56.645 --> 00:15:00.081
The Bear Pianist is playing.

00:15:00.882 --> 00:15:02.450
Oh! Look!
The bad guy!

00:15:02.450 --> 00:15:04.441
You're right.

00:15:05.654 --> 00:15:06.643
Ok!

00:15:17.599 --> 00:15:19.567
Ok, we did it!

00:15:19.567 --> 00:15:21.102
Ow. Ow. Ow.

00:15:21.102 --> 00:15:23.138
Huh?
What's that?

00:15:23.138 --> 00:15:24.127
Where?

00:15:26.374 --> 00:15:30.078
A-Are you all right?

00:15:30.078 --> 00:15:30.908
Y-Yeah.

00:15:42.824 --> 00:15:44.792
This is really getting old.

00:15:55.136 --> 00:15:57.900
I hope this is all right.

00:15:58.139 --> 00:16:00.141
Now what?

00:16:00.141 --> 00:16:02.006
What's this?

00:16:05.714 --> 00:16:07.215
Oh! The snow for the play?

00:16:07.215 --> 00:16:08.083
Thank you.

00:16:08.083 --> 00:16:10.151
Your piano playing is
a light in my heart.

00:16:10.151 --> 00:16:11.186
Yay! Yay! Whee!
Your piano playing is
a light in my heart.

00:16:11.186 --> 00:16:14.986
Yay! Yay! Whee!
It always brightens my heart
as I wander in the darkness...

00:16:19.561 --> 00:16:21.162
I have always...

00:16:21.162 --> 00:16:22.263
Oh, my dear!

00:16:22.263 --> 00:16:24.165
Wherefore art thou,
my beloved?

00:16:24.165 --> 00:16:26.568
Oh, my dear,
there you are!

00:16:26.568 --> 00:16:30.163
Whee!
Yay!

00:16:32.907 --> 00:16:35.899
Huh, Saga,
what're you doing?

00:16:37.178 --> 00:16:39.112
You guys.

00:16:39.581 --> 00:16:42.016
I can only stay in this
human form at night.

00:16:42.016 --> 00:16:44.119
Hmph! Watching this lazy
young man is boring!
I can only stay in this
human form at night.

00:16:44.119 --> 00:16:46.821
Hmph! Watching this lazy
young man is boring!
When morning comes,
I will turn back into a bear.

00:16:46.821 --> 00:16:48.123
When morning comes,
I will turn back into a bear.

00:16:48.123 --> 00:16:49.124
Them?

00:16:49.124 --> 00:16:50.785
What a funny fellow.

00:16:55.497 --> 00:16:59.868
Really! You were just about
to mess up the play, you know?

00:16:59.868 --> 00:17:01.870
Mess up the play?

00:17:01.870 --> 00:17:04.134
What on earth did we do?

00:17:04.706 --> 00:17:06.970
All we did was investigate!

00:17:08.743 --> 00:17:09.732
Fine.

00:17:10.011 --> 00:17:12.138
What are you doing there?

00:17:13.214 --> 00:17:15.216
Elder?

00:17:15.216 --> 00:17:19.187
Chairman, is it true
the bear ran away?

00:17:19.187 --> 00:17:20.121
Yes.

00:17:20.121 --> 00:17:21.611
That bear is dangerous!

00:17:21.923 --> 00:17:25.154
Even though it plays the piano,
it's still a wild animal!

00:17:25.593 --> 00:17:29.586
Who can say it won't
return to its wild nature?

00:17:30.031 --> 00:17:32.499
It must be destroyed!

00:17:33.268 --> 00:17:35.336
Huh? Is that... Greta?

00:17:35.336 --> 00:17:36.997
What's she doing there?

00:17:38.373 --> 00:17:43.344
Just watch. My passionate
performance will win the crowd over!

00:17:43.344 --> 00:17:45.447
But its talent is very valuable.

00:17:45.447 --> 00:17:48.143
You're too naive!

00:17:48.817 --> 00:17:50.182
A wild beast!

00:17:50.852 --> 00:17:52.319
Is always!

00:17:52.854 --> 00:17:54.253
A ferocious creature!

00:17:55.323 --> 00:17:57.992
Instead of making
it play the piano,

00:17:57.992 --> 00:18:01.189
you should take it out!
Immediately!

00:18:01.830 --> 00:18:03.058
I'm falling!

00:18:03.431 --> 00:18:04.420
Elder!

00:18:08.870 --> 00:18:10.672
S-Something's inside!

00:18:10.672 --> 00:18:11.339
Oh, no!!

00:18:11.339 --> 00:18:13.364
Get it out!
Get it out!

00:18:17.445 --> 00:18:19.047
At this rate,
the play will be ruined.

00:18:19.047 --> 00:18:21.345
Can't anyone do anything?

00:18:22.150 --> 00:18:23.742
There's no other choice.

00:18:24.752 --> 00:18:26.151
Vincent?

00:18:28.156 --> 00:18:30.283
That weird guy from before?

00:18:30.592 --> 00:18:35.086
No! Stop! No!

00:18:35.864 --> 00:18:39.857
Don't look at me!
Help me!

00:18:47.275 --> 00:18:49.110
Wh-What's this?

00:18:49.110 --> 00:18:52.113
Even the hunters can't stop
themselves from having fun,

00:18:52.113 --> 00:18:55.605
and dancing when they
hear my piano playing!!

00:18:56.885 --> 00:18:59.854
Perfect, Vincent.
Smart move!

00:18:59.854 --> 00:19:01.651
Oh, but, but...

00:19:07.161 --> 00:19:09.130
Whee, how fun!

00:19:09.130 --> 00:19:10.119
Hey!

00:19:29.617 --> 00:19:31.141
Oh!
The string?

00:19:34.856 --> 00:19:36.619
Oh, I can't take it anymore!

00:19:46.868 --> 00:19:48.631
Now, finally.

00:19:52.106 --> 00:19:55.098
Wh-What did I just do?

00:19:55.810 --> 00:19:57.471
How's that, Chairman?

00:19:57.645 --> 00:20:00.381
Are you still going to listen
to the hunters about me?

00:20:00.381 --> 00:20:05.186
N-No. You're quite
a bear, after all.

00:20:05.186 --> 00:20:08.622
I'll tell the hunters.

00:20:15.129 --> 00:20:19.657
Good grief! It looks like
we managed somehow.

00:20:20.535 --> 00:20:22.670
Even if it was for
the sake of the play,

00:20:22.670 --> 00:20:24.405
to treat the piano
so recklessly...

00:20:24.405 --> 00:20:27.374
It's not how a
pianist would act!

00:20:31.145 --> 00:20:33.348
What was with Greta, anyway?

00:20:33.348 --> 00:20:34.440
Who knows?

00:20:34.682 --> 00:20:37.151
I was so moved.

00:20:37.151 --> 00:20:40.088
I get it!
The bear's performance!

00:20:40.088 --> 00:20:42.557
This was it,
wasn't it, Elder?

00:20:42.557 --> 00:20:44.081
What I was missing.

00:20:44.325 --> 00:20:47.195
Huh? Yes, that's right, Turmeric.
I'm glad you realized.

00:20:47.195 --> 00:20:50.865
That's exactly what
I wanted to say.

00:20:50.865 --> 00:20:52.867
Ok. Now I've got an
image for a new cloud.
Ginger,
did you get it, too? Huh?

00:20:52.867 --> 00:20:54.102
Ok. Now I've got an
image for a new cloud.
Ginger,
did you get it, too? Huh?

00:20:54.102 --> 00:20:55.967
Wait, Turmeric!
Ginger,
did you get it, too? Huh?

00:20:57.305 --> 00:21:03.111
I-It appears that I must make use
of my talents in areas other than acting.

00:21:03.111 --> 00:21:06.547
So after today I'm resigning
my membership from this troupe.

00:21:06.547 --> 00:21:08.316
I... I see.

00:21:08.316 --> 00:21:10.318
That's too bad,
really too bad...

00:21:10.318 --> 00:21:11.979
Well, good-bye.

00:21:15.123 --> 00:21:17.191
Chairman,
did you see the girl?

00:21:17.191 --> 00:21:18.419
From the coffee shop?

00:21:18.559 --> 00:21:20.652
I think she left already.

00:21:22.130 --> 00:21:24.291
I see.
She's gone, huh?

00:21:24.766 --> 00:21:27.135
The bear was great today!

00:21:27.135 --> 00:21:31.139
People who play the piano
are called "pianists," right?

00:21:31.139 --> 00:21:34.131
Then he's a great pianist!

00:21:34.375 --> 00:21:37.708
No! He's not a pianist at all!

00:21:37.845 --> 00:21:38.834
What?

00:21:39.080 --> 00:21:41.716
But it was really fun.

00:21:41.716 --> 00:21:45.083
Being a pianist isn't a
matter of just being fun!

00:21:45.653 --> 00:21:48.679
Besides, he even
broke a piano string.

00:21:48.823 --> 00:21:51.659
I can't stand that
sort of piano playing.

00:21:51.659 --> 00:21:52.648
Saga.

00:21:57.131 --> 00:21:58.860
That time,

00:22:03.771 --> 00:22:07.832
I wonder if he
could see us.

00:22:21.122 --> 00:22:25.560
Tsuki no negai

00:22:25.560 --> 00:22:29.097
Mizu ni tokete

00:22:29.097 --> 00:22:34.368
Shiroi namiki-michi mitsuketa

00:22:34.368 --> 00:22:39.440
Hoshi-kuzu no uta

00:22:39.440 --> 00:22:47.882
Nana-iro no hashi o wataru kaze

00:22:47.882 --> 00:22:53.087
Shitte ita yo ne

00:22:53.087 --> 00:22:57.080
Kimochi tsunagu ureshisa

00:22:57.859 --> 00:23:00.094
Sugar Snow

00:23:00.094 --> 00:23:08.102
Kona-yuki mau machi ni yagate

00:23:08.102 --> 00:23:13.107
Kirei na hana saku kisetsu ni

00:23:13.107 --> 00:23:18.204
Anata o omou

00:23:20.114 --> 00:23:24.452
Kokoro o tokasu

00:23:24.452 --> 00:23:28.422
ai wa, yume wa

00:23:28.422 --> 00:23:35.123
sono mune ni aruno

00:23:39.934 --> 00:23:41.068
Preview of Next Episode

00:23:41.068 --> 00:23:42.303
Preview of Next Episode
I can't believe it!

00:23:42.303 --> 00:23:44.972
Preview of Next Episode
How can he play
the piano like that?

00:23:44.972 --> 00:23:50.077
Hmm, it's strange.
Can he see me, I wonder?

00:23:50.077 --> 00:23:54.081
He's not a real pianist.
I know it, but...

00:23:54.081 --> 00:23:55.082
Still...

00:23:55.082 --> 00:23:58.540
I can't stop thinking
about Vincent.

00:23:58.719 --> 00:24:02.621
"A Little Snow Fairy Sugar"
The Next Episode Is
"My Favorite Piano."

00:24:02.790 --> 00:24:06.351
The stay-close-to-Mr. Bear
plan begins!
